<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's MKB bank profits soar to 9.2 bln forints. [CORRECTED 13:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>Hungary's MKB bank profits soar to 9.2 bln forints. [CORRECTED 13:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996, ending December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					Jan-Dec 1996   As percentage of</p>
<p>	    the 1995 figures</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   9,857.9		147.91</p>
<p>    Pre-tax result	     9,216.0		151.06</p>
<p>    Net interest income     13,367.7		117.40</p>
<p>    Banking expenses	   6,174.9		121.93</p>
<p>    Dividends received	   385.7		152.85</p>
<p>Income from other banking</p>
<p>    activities		  11,186.3		141.68</p>
<p>Expenses of other banking</p>
<p>    activities		   6,882.6		163.26</p>
<p>Profits from non-banking</p>
<p>    activities			54.1		-66.92</p>
<p>    Other income		 5,073.4		 86.09</p>
<p>    Other expenses	     7,097.8		 74.85</p>
<p>    Extraordinary income	 696.0 loss	 144.10</p>
<p>NOTE - MKB, whose shares trade on the Budapest over-the-counter market, is among the three biggest Hungarian commercial banks in terms of assets. It is controlled by Germany's Bayerische LB (corrects from West LB).</p>
<p>The figures are unaudited, unconsolidated and are calculated on the basis of an 18 percent tax rate.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
